{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.LeptonMassTowerCanonical","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.LeptonMassTowerCanonical","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.lepton_indices_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.lepton_indices_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L205-L208","doc":"**SPECIAL CASE.** The lepton tower index is injective — distinct\nleptons have distinct torus-knot indices. Already proved sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.muon_electron_ratio_from_tower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.muon_electron_ratio_from_tower","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L198-L203","doc":"**CONDITIONAL.** If the lepton tower holds, then the muon-to-electron\nratio is determined by the torus-knot step T(2,3) → T(2,5) via\nthe figure-eight knot transition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.lepton_tower_index_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.lepton_tower_index_injective","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L189-L192","doc":"The index is injective on leptons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.lepton_tower_index","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.lepton_tower_index","kind":"def","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L177-L187","doc":"**THEOREM.** The lepton-tower index walk: leptons are indexed by\nnatural numbers via the T(2, 2m+1) torus-knot tower\n(electron m=1, cinquefoil m=2, septafoil m=3). The muon m=2\ncandidate is structurally consistent with PR #1153's P_m / Q_m\nframework; the canonical paper identification (muon = 4_1) is\nNOT in this torus-knot tower and is the framework's structural\noutlier per docs/audits/2026-05-25-lepton-tower-structure.md. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.lepton_mass_ratio_im_q_invariance_at_LO","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.lepton_mass_ratio_im_q_invariance_at_LO","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L168-L174","doc":"**CONJECTURE (Im(q) invariance at LO).** The lepton mass ratio\nvia modulus projection is invariant under q ↦ q̄ at leading order.\nStatement-only; full proof requires complex extension + explicit F_ℓ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.figure_eight_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.figure_eight_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L133-L166","doc":"Figure-eight (σ_1 σ_2⁻¹)² reduction in H_3(q).\nRequires:\n- σ_1, σ_2 satisfy Hecke relation: σ_i² = h σ_i + 1\n- σ_2⁻¹ = σ_2 - h (Hecke definition)\n- braid relation: σ_1 σ_2 σ_1 = σ_2 σ_1 σ_2\n\nResult: (σ_1 σ_2⁻¹)² = σ_2 σ_1 - h² σ_1 σ_2 - h σ_2 + h³ σ_1 + h²\n\nPROOF DEFERRED. The full expansion requires a non-commutative\nring setting (CommRing makes braid relation imply σ_1 = σ_2,\ntrivialising the theorem); statement is in CommRing for\nLean-syntactic compatibility with the rest of the file, but\nthe actual proof requires `Ring R` + `noncomm_ring` tactic\nor explicit calc steps with the braid relation. Numerical\ncorrectness verified at q_0 in\ndocs/audits/2026-05-24-m-mu-over-m-e-operator-rederivation.md.\n\nThe pattern of the proof:\n1. σ_1 (σ_2 - h) = σ_1 σ_2 - h σ_1\n2. expand (σ_1 σ_2 - h σ_1)²\n3. apply braid σ_1 σ_2 σ_1 = σ_2 σ_1 σ_2\n4. apply Hecke σ_1² = h σ_1 + 1, σ_2² = h σ_2 + 1\n5. simplify\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.FigureEightReductionConjecture.reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.FigureEightReductionConjecture.reduction","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.FigureEightReductionConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.FigureEightReductionConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L130-L130","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.FigureEightReductionConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.FigureEightReductionConjecture","kind":"class","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L129-L131","doc":"**CONJECTURE.** Figure-eight reduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.torus_knot_odd_reduction_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.torus_knot_odd_reduction_exists","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L93-L127","doc":"**THEOREM (corollary).** Generalisation of trefoil reduction\nto all odd-index torus knots T(2, 2m+1) = σ_1^(2m+1).\nBy induction on m: σ^(2m+1) = P_m · σ + Q_m where P_m, Q_m\nare polynomials in h satisfying P_{m+1} = h · P_m + Q_m,\nQ_{m+1} = P_m. This connects to PR #1153's P_m / Q_m\nframework for the lepton tower (electron m=1, also implicitly\nhigher odd-index leptons).\n\nStatement only; full induction proof is straightforward but\nmulti-step; deferred. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.trefoil_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.trefoil_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L80-L91","doc":"**THEOREM (algebraic).** Trefoil σ_1³ reduction in H_2(q):\nσ_1³ = (h² + 1) σ_1 + h\nwhere h ∈ R and the Hecke relation σ² = h σ + 1 is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.heckeH","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L70-L78","doc":"Hecke amplitude `h = q - q⁻¹`.\n\n§7c: `q` is carried as a **unit** `q : Rˣ`, so `q⁻¹` is the ring\nelement `↑q⁻¹` of `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` rather than a field inverse — the rest\nof this file is already generic over `[CommRing R]`, and this\ndefinition now matches it.  Every field instance is recovered by\n`Units.mk0 q hq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.lepton_mass_ratio_electron_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.lepton_mass_ratio_electron_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L63-L68","doc":"**THEOREM.** The electron mass ratio is the multiplicative identity\nby calibration convention (CAL-1 sets the mass unit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.lepton_mass_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.lepton_mass_ratio","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L48-L61","doc":"Conjectural lepton-mass categorical formula `F_ℓ(q)`.\n\nFor the electron, by calibration convention `F_electron(q) = 1`\n(electron is CAL-1, the mass unit). For muon and tau, the formula\nis conjectural per `conj:lepton-mass-tower-canonical`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:lepton-mass-tower-canonical","label":"conj:lepton-mass-tower-canonical","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonMassRatioConjecture.tau_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonMassRatioConjecture.tau_ratio","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonMassRatioConjecture.muon_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonMassRatioConjecture.muon_ratio","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonMassRatioConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonMassRatioConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonMassRatioConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonMassRatioConjecture","kind":"class","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L43-L46","doc":"**CONJECTURE.** Lepton mass ratio for muon and tau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.instReprLeptonType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.instReprLeptonType","kind":"instance","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.instReprLeptonType.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.instReprLeptonType.repr","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.instDecidableEqLeptonType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.instDecidableEqLeptonType","kind":"instance","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonType.tau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonType.tau","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonType.muon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonType.muon","kind":"ctor","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonType.electron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonType.electron","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonMassTowerCanonical.LeptonType","kind":"inductive","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-mass-tower-canonical.lean#L36-L41","doc":"Lepton enumeration. ","signatureChunk":0}]}